flowchart LR
  subgraph win["Console window: React"]
    sidebar[Sidebar panels]
    notes[Notification items]
    term[Terminal commands]
    addr[Address bar]
    bc[BrowserController]
    hist[(Request history)]
    mpc[MainPanelViewController]
    lc[LayoutContent]
    res[Resource components]
  end
  be[Node back end]

  sidebar -->|open request| bc
  notes -->|open request| bc
  term -->|open request| bc
  addr -->|open request| bc
  bc -->|push or move| hist
  bc -->|browser-load event| be
  be -->|broadcast| mpc
  mpc -->|onConsoleBrowserLoadEvent| lc
  lc -->|switch on first segment| res

%% tip: Sidebar panels :: Circuits and dashboard panels open resources via makeSidebarBrowserRequest.
%% tip: Notification items :: Circuit and WTF-threshold notifications open the circuit.
%% tip: Terminal commands :: The in-app terminal can navigate too.
%% tip: Address bar :: BrowserLayout — type a URI, or use back/forward.
%% tip: BrowserController :: One shared instance per window (factory name LAYOUT_BROWSER).
%% tip: Request history :: Up to 10 requests; back/forward move an index.
%% tip: MainPanelViewController :: Listens for the load event on LayoutContent's behalf.
%% tip: LayoutContent :: Holds the current resource in state and renders the matching component.
%% tip: Resource components :: Journal, Circuit, Retro, Flow, Dashboard, Control, Play, Moovie, Tools, Terminal.
%% tip: open request :: A string like open::/journal/me — action, "::", URI.
%% tip: browser-load event :: WINDOW_CONSOLE_BROWSER_LOAD, dispatched with echo.
%% tip: broadcast :: Main re-sends the event to every window.
%% tip: switch on first segment :: /journal/me → JournalResource; terminal, play, moovie hide the address bar.
